<p>Why do they want to help him flesh out his creation?</p>
<hr />
<p>I think my biggest concern here is that there's not a lot of narrative to this: there's like, a kinda resigned acceptance that people will end up in the dream world and then a vague nod towards historical britain and I'm left wondering what the narrative purpose of it all is. Like, you mention there are logs of these journeys: what's linking the logs together? How does this combine to create a coherent arc told through successive logs?</p>
<p>It doesn't necessarily have to be a narrative arc here: this feels like it'd be really ripe for some kind of emotional arc in the SCP, perhaps him coming to terms with being contained, or perhaps some kind of grappling with like, getting old and him trying to recapture lost youth before realising he can't fully or something like that, y'know?</p>
</div>
