<p>1. Yeah, I mean, that's really all the risk is, the effect goes further, but lets say the foundation lets this happen, the man may become violent and knock off anyone who enters the dream, which is now accessible from several miles away. I didn't have room in the pitch, but during initial recovery (which was in a city,) there were several people in the AOE who did not have anything to wake them up and suffered from extreme malnutrition after being trapped in the dream until having their consciousness ejected from the dream while the SCP was lifted (helicopter) to site 88.</p>
<p>D-Class are not allowed near the anomaly because of the risk presented by having potentially dangerous criminals near a person that must be kept happy (even if there are D-Class with good records, foundation personnel can be trusted more with handling containment. D-Class may have been further considered if the SCP was not so easily handled by the staff.) And sedation will not transport the person's consciousness to the dream, only sleep.</p>
<p>This is also not a story where the Foundation is bending a knee to the whims of an anomaly, they could just shoot his body if they wanted to, rather, personnel follow a relatively strict code on keepings certain things hidden from the SCP and how to interact with him for &quot;maximum happiness.&quot;</p>
