<p><em>Responding to PM request</em></p>
<p>Wow, boy howdy, this is a really long thread with a lot of commitment, a lot of ideas and a lot of passion.</p>
<p>I don't really know how to offer my own take on this or how helpful it'll be, but I'll crit as best as I can with the concept pitch itself along with your response to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cyvstvi13" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6004508); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6004508&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605725653" alt="Cyvstvi13" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6004508)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cyvstvi13" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6004508); return false;">Cyvstvi13</a></span>'s crit.</p>
<p>I also peeked a little at some of the other crits for some extra background.</p>
<p>Well.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+Let's&nbsp;do&nbsp;it!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Let's&nbsp;do&nbsp;it</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Okay, I'll treat this as a normal crit and just offer my own take on this. I'll also keep it short so I don't accidentally repeat what everyone else has said.</p>
<p>I found the initial <strong>Elevator Pitch</strong> very bland, some person pulls people into their dreams. They're comatose, yeah, but pulling people into dream worlds isn't anything new. Keeping people in a pocket reality, also pretty done.</p>
<p>I <em>do</em> really like the idea of the wife being stuck in the dream reality with the comatose husband as lovers trapped in a personal love nest (or coping mechanism or whatever), but like&#8230;how on earth do you plan to show this in an article?</p>
<p>You can easily headcanon an Onerei-trained researcher with some device that lets you record dream brainwaves and convert them into videos, but then what? A series of emotional interviews, I feel like would be inadequate.</p>
<p>Also, why would they just include some civilian woman in their operations? The Foundation doesn't care about emotions. The most realistic thing they'd end up doing is amnesticizing her (as <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/forbiddenquest" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6394686); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6394686&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605725653" alt="forbiddenquest" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6394686)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/forbiddenquest" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6394686); return false;">forbiddenquest</a></span> has already stated) stuffing him in a containment cell away from 'nearby' civilians and just putting him on life support. Maybe go in and interview him here and there to make sure he's&#8230;'fine' I guess? For a comatose person with a dream reality.</p>
<p>This is the one time in existence I've ever recommended turning something into a Tale instead, not because Tales don't work or that I dislike them or any personal bias against them.</p>
<p>I just can't think of a way you could make this work via an emotionless post-mortem scientific document.</p>
<p>Writing this out via actual prose would be the perfect way to show the woman wanting to take care of him before dying and just being trapped in there with him. Shoehorning personnel in there for interviews would be <em>way</em> too forced and awkward.</p>
<p>Also, even with all this in mind, this reads like the concept pitch for&#8230;probably like a weird anime or studio ghibli movie? I think? Not really an SCP.</p>
<p>I love the element of a spouse trying to take care of another spouse in a dream world sub-reality, but thinking about it now, I'm also getting Inception vibes from this.</p>
<p>Now I'm just rambling.</p>
<p>I apologise if this was harsh, but this entire thing was a mess to sift through what with all the pre-existing crits and kinda weirdly distributed info.</p>
<p>I do bid you the best of luck with this because I like the passion I'm feeling from this as well as the dedication, but this needs a rework of some kind that fits in with the Foundation format and presented as&#8230;less messy.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

